# Goal implement Nearest Neighbor's heuristic with Simulated Annealing
# Nearest Neighbor survey's the closes nodes
# Simulated annealing helps escape local minima by adding in some randomness (sometimes accepting worse solutions) to exploring the search space 
# - Starts with high temperature (more likely to start in a random direction) then the temperature cools to be more predictable when close to the goal

# Dataset: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mexwell/traveling-salesman-problem
# We will select the first index of the dataset to be our starting city
# Can also test with a home base being at (0, 0). 